<title>FRANCE: Lyonnaise unit sells property asset.</title>
<headline>Lyonnaise unit sells property asset.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duminvest, a wholly-owned unit of Lyonnaise des Eaux, has sold its 85 percent holding in Nevis Hotel Development Ltd to U.S.-based Maritz &amp; Wolff for $78 million, Lyonnaise said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said it expected a capital gain from the sale to reduce the group's losses in the property sector this year from 1995 levels.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale is part of Lyonnaise's strategy to reduce property holdings,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
</text>
